  ```
- Resolve `attributed_owned: Option<AttributedString>`:
  ```rust
  let bound_attributed = node.attributed_binding.map(|sid| self.store.get(sid)).and_then(|v| v.to_attributed().cloned());
  let attributed_borrowed: Option<&AttributedString> = bound_attributed.as_ref().or(node.attributed_text.as_ref());
  ```
  This needs owned for binding because store returns value clone. Could store `SignalValue` and borrow; simpler:
  ```rust
  let bound_value: Option<SignalValue> = node.attributed_binding.map(|sid| self.store.get(sid));
  let attributed_borrowed: Option<&AttributedString> = match (&bound_value, &node.attributed_text) {
      (Some(v), _) => v.to_attributed(),
      (None, Some(a)) => Some(a),
      _ => None,
  };
  ```
- Determine `text_borrowed`: If attributed is present, we don't emit SET_TEXT; but still compute plain fallback? For `text_changed` we should compare plain text? We need separate logic.
  - `attributed_changed` compare prev `.attributed` value to `attributed_borrowed`. For mount: `None => attributed_borrowed.is_some()`.
  - `text_changed`: if attributed present, no SET_TEXT; when attributed absent, compare plain text. Also when previous had attributed and now plain, emit SET_TEXT (even if text same) to clear rich formatting. So:
    ```rust
    let text_mode = attributed_borrowed.is_some();
    let text_changed = match &prev {
      Some(p) => {
        let prev_attributed = p.attributed.is_some();
        if text_mode {
          // only attributed changes handled separately
          false
        } else {
          prev_attributed || p.text.as_deref() != text_borrowed
        }
      }
      None => !text_mode && text_borrowed.is_some(),
    };
    ```
    But plain `text_borrowed` should be `Some(attributed.text())` when attributed. For snapshot `text`, store the plain text always. If attributed is present, `text_borrowed` = attributed.text() (for snapshot). If no attributed, normal.
  - On mount: if attributed present, call `guest.set_attributed_text` and omit SET_TEXT. If plain, SET_TEXT.
  - On delta:
    - if attributed_changed: if Some -> emit SET_ATTRIBUTED_TEXT; if None -> emit SET_TEXT if text_borrowed is Some (clearing).
    - else if text_changed (plain): emit SET_TEXT.
  - Need arena offset reuse: `SnapshotNode.attributed: Option<(AttributedString, u32)>`. If attributed unchanged, reuse offset but no op. If changed, allocate.
- Snapshot update:
  - `attributed_snapshot = match attributed_emit { Some(...) => ..., None => prev_attributed.unwrap_or(None) }`.
  - Similarly `text` snapshot: always `text_borrowed.map(...)`.
- Dependency recording: `attributed_binding` -> `Dep::AttributedText`.
- `emit_cell` add arm.
- Zero-alloc: comparing AttributedString no alloc. `text_borrowed` from attributed no alloc. Good.
- `SnapshotNode` PartialEq derive: AttributedString PartialEq. Good.

Need to be careful: `attributed_borrowed` borrows `bound_value` or `node.attributed_text`; both live until end of function. Fine.

- When attributed present, the plain `text_borrowed` should come from attributed text so snapshot stores correct plain text. We can define:
  ```rust
  let text_borrowed: Option<&str> = match attributed_borrowed {
      Some(a) => Some(a.text()),
      None => match (&bound_text, &node.component) {...}
  };
  ```
- `attributed_changed` compare:
  ```rust
  let attributed_changed = match &prev {
      Some(p) => p.attributed.as_ref().map(|(v,_)| v) != attributed_borrowed,
      None => attributed_borrowed.is_some(),
  };
  ```
  Comparing `Option<&AttributedString>` works? `p.attributed.as_ref().map(|(v, _)| v)` yields Option<&AttributedString>; compare to Option<&AttributedString>. `PartialEq` for Option<&T> works. Good.
- But if previous had attributed and now plain, `attributed_changed` true (Some->None). We then emit `SET_TEXT` (text_borrowed). Good.
- `text_changed`:
  ```rust
  let text_changed = if attributed_borrowed.is_some() {
      false
  } else {
      match &prev {
          Some(p) => p.attributed.is_some() || p.text.as_deref() != text_borrowed,
          None => text_borrowed.is_some(),
      }
  };
  ```
  If prev attributed and now plain, text_changed true, emit SET_TEXT. If prev plain and now attributed, text_changed false (attributed handled). Good.
  If both plain, normal.
  If both attributed, text_changed false.
- On mount: if attributed Some -> emit SET_ATTRIBUTED_TEXT, else SET_TEXT.
- On delta: `if attributed_changed { if let Some(a) = attributed_borrowed { emit set_attributed_text; } else if text_changed { ... } }` But if attributed changed Some->None, we need SET_TEXT. If attributed changed None->Some, emit attributed. If Some->Some, emit attributed. Then also text_changed could be true independently? We set text_changed false when attributed present; when attributed absent and prev attributed, true. So:
  ```rust
  if attributed_changed {
      match attributed_borrowed {
        Some(a) => { guest.set_attributed_text(...); *out += 1; }
        None => if let Some(t)=text_borrowed { guest.set_text(...); *out +=1; }
      }
  } else if text_changed { ... }
  ```
  This works. But when both prev/current attributed and text changed, attributed_changed true because AttributedString differs, emit attributed. Good.
- `attributed_emit` Option<(AttributedString,u32)> for snapshot:
  - On mount Some -> alloc and push, set Some((a.clone(), offset)).
  - On delta if attributed_changed and Some -> alloc/push.
  - If attributed unchanged -> keep prev.
  - If None -> None.
- To avoid borrowing issues, compute after prev taken.

Also note: `text_borrowed` when attributed present uses `a.text()`; if attributed text is empty and plain text empty, still emit attributed if it has runs? Runs over empty invalid; no. Fine.

