Add functions near setNodeText. Also add guard in setNodeText. Implement:

```ts
const ATTRIBUTED_DECODER = new TextDecoder();

function applyAttributedText(el: HTMLElement, value: AttributedText): void {
  const container = el.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".pathland-text") ?? el;
  el.classList.add("pathland-rich-text");
  const nodes: Node[] = [];
  for (const segment of attributedSegments(value)) {
    const text = ATTRIBUTED_DECODER.decode(value.textBytes.subarray(segment.start, segment.end));
    const css = runCss(segment.attributes);
    if (!css && !segment.link) { nodes.push(document.createTextNode(text)); continue; }
    const node = document.createElement(segment.link ? "a" : "span");
    if (segment.link) (node as HTMLAnchorElement).setAttribute("href", segment.link);
    if (css) node.setAttribute("style", css);
    node.textContent = text;
    nodes.push(node);
  }
  container.replaceChildren(...nodes);
  // If the TEXT element itself changed tag? no.
  void el;
}
```
But `document.createElement` may not exist in SSR? This is DOM client only. Fine. To use the renderer's document, use `el.ownerDocument`. Better:
```ts
const doc = el.ownerDocument;
```
Use `doc.createTextNode`, `doc.createElement`.

`runCss(attributes)`:
- iterate; map; collect underline/strike.
- F32 values: `new DataView(new ArrayBuffer(4))`? Use helper `f32FromBits` imported? Search.

