Emitter: add attributed emission in `emitNode`, `registerNodeBindings`, `reconcileNode`, `emitSubtreeInto`, `currentText` maybe. Need a helper `currentAttributed(node)`.

- `emitNode`: after text, if attributed -> `sink.setAttributedText(node.id, attributed)` (and skip setText?). Current code:
```kotlin
val text = node.textValue()
if (text != null && text.isNotEmpty()) sink.setText(node.id, text)
```
Change:
```kotlin
val attributed = node.attributedValue()
if (attributed != null) sink.setAttributedText(...) else { text... }
```
- `registerNodeBindings`: add `attributedBinding?.let { if (!isConstant) effect { val value = it.get(); if (value != node.attributedText) { node.attributedText = value; node.text = value.text; begin/setAttributed/end } } }`
  Note `Signal<AttributedString>` may be ConstantSignal if created with `Signals.constant`? Signals.constant likely only for String? It's generic.
- `reconcileNode`: compare `old.attributedText` vs `fresh.attributedValue()`. But old's static field updated? In the existing text reconcile, they use `old.text` and `currentText(fresh)`. For attributed:
```kotlin
val oldAttr = old.attributedValue()
val freshAttr = currentAttributed(fresh)
if (oldAttr != freshAttr) { ops.add { freshAttr?.let { sink.setAttributedText } ?: freshText... } }
```
But if switching attributed -> plain, need `setText`. Handle:
```kotlin
if (oldAttr != freshAttr) {
  if (freshAttr != null) ops.add { sink.setAttributedText(id, freshAttr) }
  else { val t = currentText(fresh); if (t != null) ops.add { sink.setText(id, t) } }
}
```
Also existing plain text diff would also emit SET_TEXT if text differs. Need avoid duplicate when attributed present. Change the plain diff to only when `freshAttr == null`. And if old had attributed but fresh plain with same text, need emit SET_TEXT; the `oldText` comparison uses `old.text`, which may equal. So add a condition: `if (freshAttr == null && (oldAttr != null || oldText != freshText))`. Let's restructure in reconcile:
```kotlin
val oldAttr = old.attributedText
val freshAttr = currentAttributed(fresh)
val oldText = old.text
val freshText = currentText(fresh)
if (oldAttr != freshAttr) {
  if (freshAttr != null) ops.add { sink.setAttributedText(id, freshAttr) }
  else if (freshText != null && freshText.isNotEmpty()) ops.add { sink.setText(id, freshText) }
} else if (freshAttr == null && oldText != freshText) {
  ops.add { sink.setText(id, freshText!!) }
}
```
- `emitSubtreeInto`: if attributed, setAttributedText else setText.
- `currentText`: already exists; add `currentAttributed`.
- Also when mounting with attributed, `node.text` may be null; set `node.text` in Views. Good.

