parts.text:
Modify:
- `emitNode`: `attributed != null && !attributed.isPlain` -> setAttributed; else text = attributed?.text ?: node.textValue(); if not empty setText.
- `registerNodeBindings` attributed effect: if value.isPlain -> setText; else setAttributed.
- `reconcileNode`: compare; if freshAttributed != null and !isPlain -> attributed; else text = freshAttributed?.text ?: freshText. Need handle transition. Current `oldAttributed` and `freshAttributed` compare using `AttributedString` equality. For reactive plain strings, freshAttributed is a plain AttributedString; oldAttributed maybe plain/rich; equality works. Emit:
  ```kotlin
  val rich = freshAttributed?.takeUnless { it.isPlain }
  if (oldAttributed != freshAttributed) {
     if (rich != null) setAttributed else { val text = freshAttributed?.text ?: freshText; setText }
  } else if (rich == null && oldText != freshText && freshText != null) { setText }
  ```
  But if oldAttributed==freshAttributed plain and oldText != freshText? `oldAttributed` plain contains text, equality includes text; if text changed, attributed differs. So fine. The second branch handles plain text bindings without attributed.
- `emitSubtreeInto`: same as emitNode.
- `currentText` for attributed plain? Not needed.

Also `PathlandNode.text` for static markdown parsed rich: `attributedTextView` sets `node.text = value.text`; good. For reactive computed, `attributedTextView` sets text initial.

Add helper `effectiveText(node)`? Could just inline.

