Add `prev_markdown_source` extraction and snapshot fields. For text when markdown unchanged, `prev_text` reused because text_changed false. For markdown changed rich, text_changed false (attributed present) and prev_text reused; but prev text may be previous plain text, not the new parsed text! Wait: when markdown changed rich, `attributed_borrowed` Some -> `text_changed=false`, so `prev_text` is set to `p.text` (old text) and snapshot `text` becomes old text, not new parsed text. The snapshot's `text` is used for `text_changed` diagnostics and for plain fallback; for attributed rich, it should be the parsed plain text. We need special handling: when markdown and attributed_changed (rich), snapshot `text` should be `attributed.text()`. Similarly when explicit attributed changes, the existing code had `text_changed=false` and `prev_text` reuse; but for explicit attributed, snapshot text wasn't used for comparison? It stores plain text but stale; maybe existing bug. For markdown, we need correct snapshot text for future transitions.
- We can set `let text = if markdown && attributed_borrowed.is_some() { Some(attributed_borrowed.unwrap().text().to_owned()) } else { ... existing ... }`. But when markdown unchanged rich, `attributed_borrowed` is None (parsed skipped) and `prev_text` reused; fine.
- When explicit attributed changes, also set text from attributed. We can generalize: if `attributed_borrowed.is_some()` and `attributed_changed`, use attributed text. But `attributed_borrowed` for markdown changed rich is Some; for unchanged none. For explicit attributed unchanged, `prev_text` reused; okay. So:
  ```rust
  let text = if attributed_changed {
      match attributed_borrowed { Some(v)=>Some(v.text().to_owned()), None=>text_borrowed.map(...) }
  } else { prev_text... or text_borrowed... };
  ```
  But if attributed_changed None (rich->plain), text_borrowed is Some(raw/plain), use it. Good.
  For mount `prev=None`, text_changed may be false if attributed present; `prev_text` None -> fallback `text_borrowed` (which is attributed text) good.
  For markdown changed rich, attributed_changed true -> use attributed text good.
  For explicit attributed changed rich, same.
  For markdown unchanged rich, attributed_changed false, prev_text Some old parsed text, reuse good.
- So modify text snapshot:
  ```rust
  let text = if attributed_changed && attributed_borrowed.is_some() {
      attributed_borrowed.map(|v| v.text().to_owned())
  } else {
      match prev_text { Some(t)=>Some(t), None=>text_borrowed.map(...) }
  };
  ```
  But if attributed_changed false and attributed_borrowed Some (mount? prev None -> attributed_changed true) okay.
- `markdown_source`:
  ```rust
