Change to best-effort multiple locations:
```java
File base = new File(System.getProperty("user.dir"));
File devDir = new File(base, "../../rust/target/debug");
if (!devLib.isFile()) devDir = new File(base.getParentFile(), "../rust/target/debug");
```
From `lib/java/pathland-view-core`, `../../rust` = `lib/rust`. Good. From repo root user.dir? `../../rust` wrong; fallback maybe. Use `base` candidates. Keep simple: `new File(base, "../../rust/target/debug")`. Tests use java.library.path. Fine.

